  {
   "id": "root",
   "x": 133,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Abnormal movement, power NORMAL: cerebellum or basal ganglia?",
   "lines": [
    "both are SIDE LOOPS: cortex → loop → thalamus → cortex · both also project to the brainstem",
    "no upper motor neurons of their own, so NOT an upper motor neuron disorder",
    "cerebellum: corrects errors + learns skills · basal ganglia: release wanted, suppress unwanted movement"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_cb",
   "x": 45,
   "y": 156,
   "w": 540,
   "h": 96,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "CEREBELLUM: movement starts, but is INACCURATE",
   "lines": [
    "signs on the SAME side as the lesion",
    "stable or slowly improve",
    "the REPAIR SHOP: masks lesions elsewhere · its own lesions last"
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "g_bg",
   "x": 625,
   "y": 156,
   "w": 356,
   "h": 96,
   "kind": "plain",
   "title": "BASAL GANGLIA: release vs suppress is off",
   "lines": [
    "globus pallidus fires at rest → inhibits thalamus",
    "dopamine: direct pathway UP, indirect DOWN"
   ]
  },
